cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PGRR: Planning-Guided Failure-Triggered Recovery and Rejoin for Dynamic Social Navigation"
message: >-
  Please cite this software artifact and the associated archival paper record
  when it becomes available.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-04
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Charles
    email: charles.chen@example.invalid
abstract: >-
  PGRR is a ROS2 framework for failure-triggered dynamic social-navigation
  recovery. A classical planner controls nominal navigation, while an
  imitation-learned policy selects planning-masked temporary subgoals or
  interpretable recovery modes near collision risk, freezing, oscillation,
  deadlock, or planner failure. Training uses a privileged short-horizon expert
  and DAgger; deployment uses observable inputs only.
keywords:
  - robot navigation
  - social navigation
  - failure recovery
  - imitation learning
  - DAgger
  - ROS2
